    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12">

                <pb facs="0099" n="19" xml:id="pg19"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15a3/668: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-02-06T17:00:00+00:00">February 6, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 6—1:05 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>39. Delegation’s No. 36, February 5, 5 p.m. If you have delivered yesterday’s
                    message please communicate the following message from Senator Robinson to
                    Senator Swanson: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>You will have noted that the American proposal is based on your
                            suggestion that options be given so that Great Britain and the United
                            States may, if they so desire, exactly duplicate each other’s cruiser
                            fleets, ship for ship, ton for ton, and gun for gun. The whole
                            delegation joins me in thanking you for this suggestion which has
                            contributed much to the possibility of solution of this problem.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
